From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:01:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] sycl: decline SET_ROWS into PTQ1_0 and PQ2_0

supports_op checked only the source and index types of SET_ROWS, so it claimed
float -> PTQ1_0/PQ2_0 rows and set_rows then aborted on the unsupported
destination type. Neither type has a float -> quant row kernel (the converter
makes them offline), so decline the pair and let the scheduler fall back, as the
CPY check already does.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
index 761b7f9c6..06f28c054 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
@@ -6114,6 +6114,11 @@ static bool do_ggml_backend_sycl_device_supports_op(ggml_backend_dev_t dev, cons
 
         case GGML_OP_SET_ROWS:
             {
+                // PTQ1_0 and PQ2_0 have no float -> quant row kernel (the converter makes them
+                // offline), so set_rows would abort on them; decline as CPY does.
+                if (op->type == GGML_TYPE_PTQ1_0 || op->type == GGML_TYPE_PQ2_0) {
+                    return false;
+                }
                 auto res = (op->src[0]->type == GGML_TYPE_F32 || op->src[0]->type == GGML_TYPE_F16 ||
                             op->src[0]->type == GGML_TYPE_BF16) &&
                            (op->src[1]->type == GGML_TYPE_I64 || op->src[1]->type == GGML_TYPE_I32);
